# Local site captures (ignored by default)
#
# These hold raw page source from third-party sites and, for HAR exports, the
# request headers of the capturing browser. They are analysis inputs, not
# source, so they stay out of git unless deliberately committed.
#
# The owner has said they are fine with captures being public; if a capture is
# worth keeping in history, `git add -f` it (or delete these lines) rather than
# relying on the default. `captures/` is the agreed drop folder; *.har is
# blocked anywhere in the tree so one cannot be committed by accident.
captures/
*.har
*.har.json
